      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An anomalous right coronary artery underwent successful percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) but exercise-induced myocardial ischemia persisted. Moreover, recurrent restenosis were angiographically documented and treated by repeat PTCA. Post-PTCA large atheroma burden not appreciable by angiography, high take-off, and tangential origin of the vessel from the aorta may be some of the mechanisms involved in myocardial ischemia persistence and restenosis of the vessel."},
